how are you doing this? We did just recently have them co-locate to more apartment-style living close together while maintaining social distancing, of course, and own rooms. But we wanted to make sure that they had a community. I think that's really important. I mean, this is is not just physically isolating. It's mentally isolating. And this also allowed us to reduce the number of shifts that are essential workers that are still on campus needed to be there. So instead of coming in five days a week when we're able to help consolidate some of the students, some of our workers were able to come in two or three times a week. So what's happening to your admissions process right now? How are you handling that?
